        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0167" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg107"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August 14, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2309.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a translation
                    of a communication received from the Tsung-li Yamên relating to the riots in
                    Fuhkien.</p>
                <p>The Yamên consents that our consul at Foochow may go to Kutien to investigate the
                    horrible massacre at that place. I have wired him that if he thought it
                    desirable and necessary he could go, and he could exercise his judgment whether
                    to go alone or with the British consul.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi></signed>.</closer>



                <xi:include href="d97-a1.xml" xpointer="d97-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
